Read and follow CLAUDE.md before anything else.

Never create plan files, scratchpads, summaries or docs unless the task asks for them by name.
No emojis anywhere.
Minimal comments in a plain human voice. No "changed by AI", no TODO litter, no explanations of obvious code.
Match the existing style of the file you are in. Avoid the over-engineered AI look: no abstractions for one caller, no defensive checks for impossible states, no new dependencies unless the task is impossible without one.
Execute directly. Do not ask for permission per step. Stop and report only when the task needs rules.py or the signer verifier changed, or when a test cannot be made to fail.
Leave zero scaffolding behind: no leftover files, no sample data outside fixtures, no phase or exercise references in shipped code.
Append the prompt contract from CLAUDE.md to your own understanding of every task: smallest clean change, no unrelated edits, run the named checks and paste the output.
